\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 YouTube\uc2  Plans A Closer Look At Content About  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Nico Grant \par \uc2 291 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 July 2022\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 5\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The video service said it would take a closer look at the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  content on its platform.\par \par \uc2 YouTube\uc2  said on Thursday that it would ban content that gave viewers instructions for ''unsafe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  methods,'' ramping up efforts to police health care content in a post-Roe era.\par \par \uc2 The world's largest video website will also remove content that ''promotes false claims about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  safety'' in the next few weeks, the company said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , citing its medical misinformation policies.\par \par \uc2 YouTube\uc2  said it would rely on ''published guidance from health authorities'' to make these determinations. In a new information panel, \uc2 YouTube\uc2  will also include a definition of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that says it is ''done by a licensed health professional.''\par \par \uc2 Since the Supreme Court's decision to overturn Roe v. Wade in June, at least eight states have banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with legislators in other states expected to propose laws to restrict access to the procedure. That has prompted supporters of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to seek workarounds for residents of those states.\par \par \uc2 With its policy decision, \uc2 YouTube\uc2  is trying to tamp down its role in storing or spreading guidance on dangerous methods. It will also provide more information from authoritative sources next to content about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Google\uc2 , \uc2 YouTube\uc2 's parent company, said this month that it would delete the location data when users visited \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics and other sensitive sites. Supporters of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and privacy groups have been concerned that authorities in states that ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  could use \uc2 Google\uc2 -held personal data to prosecute \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  cases.\par \par \uc2 The video website is trying to tamp down its role in spreading guidance on dangerous methods. (PHOTOGRAPH BY MARTIN BUREAU/AFP, VIA GETTY IMAGES) \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020220722ei7m00040\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
