\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 Ohio Man Held in Rape of Girl Who Was Focus of  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Debate\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ava Sasani \par \uc2 853 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 July 2022\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 19\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The case became a flash point in the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate after the young victim was forced to travel out of state for the procedure.\par \par \uc2 An Ohio man has been arrested and charged with the rape of a 10-year-old girl, whose travel across state lines to receive an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  captured national attention.\par \par \uc2 Gerson Fuentes, 27, was arraigned on Wednesday in Franklin County Municipal Court in Columbus, where he was charged with the rape of a child under 13 years old, a felony that can carry a lifetime prison sentence. He was being held on $2 million bond.\par \par \uc2 The arrest, and its connection to the case of the young rape victim, was first reported in The Columbus Dispatch after a public dispute over whether the story was true.\par \par \uc2 The case of the young victim became a focus of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate after the Supreme Court overturned the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  enshrined in Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 That decision triggered a wave of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions, including a law in Ohio that bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after about six weeks of pregnancy, with no exception for rape or incest. The law blocked the 10-year-old from receiving an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in her home state after her parents discovered she was pregnant.\par \par \uc2 According to a doctor familiar with her case, and testimony from a court hearing, the girl's family took her to Indiana to receive an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , where the procedure is still legal up to 22 weeks.\par \par \uc2 The girl's story, which first appeared in The Indianapolis Star, was immediately seized on by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates as the tragic but expected consequence of severe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions.\par \par \uc2 President Biden cited the story after signing an executive order on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 : ''Ten years old. Raped, six weeks pregnant. Already traumatized. Was forced to travel to another state.''\par \par \uc2 Before this week's arrest, some conservatives, including Ohio's top prosecutor, cast doubt on the story. The young girl has not been identified publicly, nor has the Ohio doctor who first treated her, and Attorney General David Yost told Fox News that his office was unaware of a case involving a 10-year-old rape victim.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Mr. Yost's office released a statement praising the arrest of Mr. Fuentes.\par \par \uc2 ''My heart aches for the pain suffered by this young child,'' the statement said. ''I am grateful for the diligent work of the Columbus Police Department in securing a confession and getting a rapist off the street.''\par \par \uc2 In an editorial published before news of the arrest, The Wall Street Journal called the case ''an unlikely story from a biased source that neatly fits the progressive narrative but can't be confirmed.'' The Journal later added an editor's note acknowledging the arrest.\par \par \uc2 In a video of the court hearing posted by the conservative news site Townhall, Detective Jeffrey Huhn testified that the victim was a 10-year-old whose mother took her to Indiana to receive an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the end of June when she was just past six weeks pregnant. Detective Huhn said in Wednesday's hearing that Mr. Fuentes confessed to raping the girl twice.\par \par \uc2 The Columbus Division of Police declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 A spokesman for U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement said Mr. Fuentes was an undocumented immigrant. A lawyer for Mr. Fuentes did not immediately respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 The timeline laid out in the police testimony matches the account provided by Dr. Caitlin Bernard, the OB/GYN who first told The Star about the case.\par \par \uc2 ''It's always shocking to me that people are surprised to hear about these stories,'' Dr. Bernard said in an interview with \uc2 The New York Times\uc2 . ''The fact that anyone would question such a story is a testament to how out of touch lawmakers and politicians are with reality.''\par \par \uc2 Dr. Bernard said such stories were unfortunately not as rare as people might think, and noted that she cared for her first underage rape victim early on in her medical residency. She has since helped several families navigate pregnancy after a child is raped, she said.\par \par \uc2 More than 7,000 girls age 14 or younger were pregnant nationwide in 2013, according to a report by the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a research organization that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. About half of those pregnancies were terminated through \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to Guttmacher.\par \par \uc2 Ohio's own public health data found that more than 500 girls and women 18 and under received an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Some anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lawmakers have approached the challenge of a Balkanized legal landscape with proposals to deter residents from traveling to other states to seek abortions. Gov. \uc2 Eric Holcomb\uc2  of Indiana called a special legislative session, scheduled for July 25, where the state may consider tighter \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions.\par \par \uc2 A 27-year-old man was arraigned on Wednesday in Franklin County Municipal Court in Columbus, Ohio, where he was charged with the rape of a 10-year-old girl. (PHOTOGRAPH BY Maddie McGarvey for The New York Times FOR THE NEW YORK TIMES) \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020220714ei7e0004b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
