\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 Biden Promised Calm, but Base Wants a Fighter\b0\par\par\uc2 By Michael D. Shear \par \uc2 1,813 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 July 2022\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 President Biden's measured approach at a time of political tumult has left him struggling to inspire his supporters and allies to action.\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON -- Forty-eight hours after a horrific mass shooting on the Fourth of July, President Biden flew to Ohio on Wednesday for a speech on pension plans.\par \par \uc2 With inflation soaring and Democrats still fuming about the Supreme Court's decision to overturn Roe v. Wade, Mr. Biden's public schedule included no events or announcements on either topic.\par \par \uc2 And in response to last week's blockbuster testimony about the Jan. 6 attack on the U.S. Capitol, Mr. Biden has said almost nothing, pledging deference to the congressional committee investigating the violent assault on American democracy.\par \par \uc2 At a moment of broad political tumult and economic distress, Mr. Biden has appeared far less engaged than many of his supporters had hoped. While many Democrats are pleading for a fighter who gives voice to their anger, Mr. Biden has chosen a more passive path -- blaming Congress, urging people to vote and avoiding heated rhetorical battles.\par \par \uc2 ''The economy seems to be running out of control. Fundamental rights are being stripped away. And the White House just isn't coming with anything,'' said Bill Neidhardt, a former spokesman for Senator \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2 , independent of Vermont.\par \par \uc2 Inside the White House, administration officials say Mr. Biden has been quick to respond to the country's crises, even if he doesn't get the credit they believe he deserves.\par \par \uc2 The president came into office promising competence and deliberative action after four years in which his predecessor governed by angry \uc2 Twitter\uc2  posts and frequent tirades. By contrast, Mr. Biden touted his sober experience as a legislator, saying it would help him bridge ideological divides. And he campaigned on knowing how to wield the authority of the presidency after serving eight years as vice president.\par \par \uc2 Early in the president's term, Mr. Biden aggressively campaigned for a trillion-dollar economic stimulus by promising $2,000 checks for every American, a robust political effort that helped energize his supporters and aided Democratic victories in Georgia to capture control of the Senate. Mr. Neidhardt said few Democrats see the same kind of energy or passion from the president now.\par \par \uc2 ''I'm not saying you have to, you know, always have a $2,000 check to wave around,'' he said. ''But you've got to do something. Some sort of action. That I think is the crux of it.''\par \par \uc2 On the big issues of the day, the president in recent months has often cited the limits of his power.\par \par \uc2 He notes that the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  has ''a primary responsibility'' to fight inflation. On guns, he insists that Congress must do more. When it comes to college tuition, voting rights, the border, competition with China and more, Mr. Biden's usual answer is that it is up to lawmakers.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court's action on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said, was a ''tragic error'' -- but not one that he can fix.\par \par \uc2 ''The only way we can secure a woman's right to choose and the balance that existed is for Congress to restore the protections of Roe v. Wade as federal law,'' Mr. Biden said. ''No executive action from the president can do that.''\par \par \uc2 Legal experts say Mr. Biden's assessment of the constraints is accurate. But critics say his measured approach simply does not meet the moment, leaving him struggling to inspire his supporters and allies to action.\par \par \uc2 Activists, elected leaders, and everyday Democratic voters say they are eager for Mr. Biden to push the legal limits. Among the ideas: Establish \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics on federal lands; demand an expansion of the Supreme Court; call for the prosecution of former President \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 ; push harder for tougher climate change regulations and legislation.\par \par \uc2 ''I don't want always-mad-trigger-happy leaders,'' Amanda Litman, a progressive activist said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  on Wednesday. ''But staying calm & barely responding when the crises in front of us are massive -- on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , guns, climate, democracy, etc -- makes us feel like *we're* the crazy ones for thinking things are bad!''\par \par \uc2 The president's White House aides and closest allies reject the Democratic criticism as little more than misinformed or misdirected complaints.\par \par \uc2 ''It's nice for Democratic leaders to come up with ideas,'' said \uc2 Cedric Richmond\uc2 , a former top White House adviser who is now working for Mr. Biden at the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2 . ''But if the ideas are illegal or if they don't work or if they place people in more harm, he's not going to do it.''\par \par \uc2 Mr. Richmond, a former member of Congress from Louisiana, lashed out at Democrats for engaging in what he called a ''circular firing squad'' and said they are buying in to Republican claims that the president's party is destined to lose the midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 ''To those Democrats that are nervous, anxious, scared, whatever you call it,'' he said, ''go out, knock some doors, win some elections.''\par \par \uc2 In Europe last week, Mr. Biden pushed world leaders to embrace a proposal to try to bring gas prices down. After months of study, Mr. Biden proposed a federal gas-tax holiday to reduce prices at the pump -- an idea popular with Democrats. When the court struck down Roe v. Wade, he issued a series of executive orders aimed at ensuring some access to health services. And last month, he helped push through the first bipartisan gun safety legislation in decades.\par \par \uc2 White House officials noted that Mr. Biden delivered a forceful speech just hours after the court's Roe decision, calling it a ''terrible, extreme decision.'' On guns, they said the president has been blunt and passionate, saying after the shootings at a Texas elementary school: ''I am sick and tired of it. We have to act. And don't tell me we can't have an impact on this carnage.''\par \par \uc2 Representative \uc2 Ro Khanna\uc2 , a Democrat from California, has called for more urgency from the White House, especially on economic issues. But he said Wednesday that the sniping about Mr. Biden from members of his own party is counterproductive and will only help Republicans win congressional elections this fall and the presidential contest in 2024.\par \par \uc2 ''The Democratic Party needs to rally around President Biden heading into the midterms and heading into the president's re-election,'' he said. ''If people have constructive ideas, they should share them. But they should do it in a spirit of strengthening this president's hand.''\par \par \uc2 Mr. Khanna said Democrats need to find constructive ways to channel their anger and frustration about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , gas prices and other issues into action. He said the party's leaders should not hesitate to take actions like imposing more regulations on guns, restoring a woman's right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or making it easier for Americans to afford everyday goods.\par \par \uc2 ''I guess my view of it is that we will have a lot more success doing that with constructive dialogue with the White House than taking potshots at the president,'' he said.\par \par \uc2 As Mr. Biden faces increased criticism, his approval ratings are taking a hit.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Monmouth University\uc2  poll released Tuesday put Mr. Biden's approval rating at 36 percent and found that a majority of Americans believe the federal government's actions are doing them harm. In a Harvard CAPS-Harris poll, 71 percent of those surveyed said they do not think the president should run for re-election.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, other Democratic politicians are jumping into what they see as a void of leadership.\par \par \uc2 In the hours after the shooting in Highland Park on Monday, Gov. \uc2 J.B. Pritzker\uc2  of Illinois captured the attention of many Democrats with a blunt proclamation: ''Be angry,'' he said, his words captured on television and later spread on social media. ''I'm furious. I'm furious that yet more innocent lives were taken by gun violence.''\par \par \uc2 Gov. \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  of California, a Democrat running for re-election, ran a television ad in Florida on Monday that gave voice to the message that many members of Mr. Biden's party wish they would hear from him.\par \par \uc2 ''Freedom, it's under attack in your state,'' Mr. Newsom said. ''Republican leaders, they're banning books, making it harder to vote, restricting speech in classrooms, even criminalizing women and doctors,'' he added, in a barely veiled political attack on \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the state's Republican governor and a possible candidate for president in 2024.\par \par \uc2 Grumbling among Democrats has been underway for weeks if not months, often focused on what they say is a failure to effectively communicate by Mr. Biden and his staff at the White House.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, \uc2 Kate Bedingfield\uc2 , the White House communications director and one of the president's longtime advisers, announced she will leave the administration soon. Top White House officials praised her work, and people close to her said she wanted to spend more time with her children after working for Mr. Biden for more than seven years.\par \par \uc2 Interviews with Democrats across the country earlier this summer showed a deep reservoir of frustration with Mr. Biden.\par \par \uc2 ''The president needs to be more aggressive,'' David Walters, the former Oklahoma governor, said. Matt Hughes, a member of the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  in North Carolina, said Mr. Biden needed to offer a ''full-throated campaign against Republican extremism.'' Radhika Nath, a former Colorado state co-chair for Mr. Sanders's 2020 campaign, cited a ''lack of energy and enthusiasm'' from the Biden administration.\par \par \uc2 ''The moment calls for inspirational leadership, not for excuses and reasons why we keep following tired old playbooks,'' she said.\par \par \uc2 But the sentiment appears to have deepened during the past several weeks, as inflation has risen, the court has ruled on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and blaring headlines describing mass shootings have become weekly occurrences.\par \par \uc2 In the face of one crisis after another, Mr. Biden has sought to explain his inability to offer solutions, in part by shifting the blame to other people or institutions.\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2 , a Utah Republican, wrote an article this week decrying what he called a ''sickness'' in Washington's politics. He praised Mr. Biden for trying to improve things but lamented his inability to do so.\par \par \uc2 ''President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is a genuinely good man,'' Mr. Romney said. ''But he has yet been unable to break through our national malady of denial, deceit, and distrust.''\par \par \uc2 Reid J. Epstein, Zolan Kanno-Youngs and \uc2 Jim Tankersley\uc2  contributed reporting.\par \par \uc2 Reid J. Epstein, Zolan Kanno-Youngs and \uc2 Jim Tankersley\uc2  contributed reporting.\par \par \uc2 President Biden has taken a passive path despite turmoil. (PHOTOGRAPH BY HAIYUN JIANG/THE NEW YORK TIMES) (A1); Critics say President Biden's measured approach simply does not meet the moment, leaving him struggling to inspire his supporters. (PHOTOGRAPH BY OLIVER CONTRERAS FOR THE NEW YORK TIMES) (A15) \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020220707ei770003i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
